APEXPROOT=../../../../..
LIB=$APEXPROOT/$objtype/lib/ape/libedg.a
EDGSRC=../../../external/edg/lib_src

# EDG's OWN C++ runtime -- operator new/delete, vtable support, static
# initialisation, pure-virtual, RTTI -- as C, translated by EDG's own
# C-generating back end.  See sys/src/external/edg/NOTE.
#
# NOT libstdc++ and nothing like it: that is the whole reason this path
# is tractable on a target with no C++ compiler, and it is why this is
# 51 small files rather than a port.
#
# THE ARCHIVE IS WHY THIS GOES FIRST.  The recorded open problem is the
# LINK model -- EDG's COMDAT emulation for vague linkage, with 3,094
# symbols named in more than one of `src''s 75 files -- and an archive
# does not have that problem: `ar' takes duplicate members happily and
# the clash only arrives when something LINKS them.  So this directory
# answers the question nothing has answered yet, "does pcc compile
# EDG's generated C at all", without the link model in the way.
#
# NO -I AND NO -D, deliberately and measured rather than assumed: each
# file here is a WHOLE LOWERED TRANSLATION UNIT and declares everything
# it uses, down to `void *memcpy(void *, const void *, unsigned long
# long)' -- that `unsigned long long' is kencc's own size_t, from
# `kencc_targ.h', so the declarations already describe this target.
# The NOTE records `gcc -fsyntax-only' over all 133 files at 0 errors
# and 0 warnings, which says the sources are clean and says nothing
# about kencc.
#
# CFLAGS is `-c' alone on purpose: every diagnostic is wanted on the
# first run through pcc, and a flag added to quiet one would hide the
# rest.  `-J' arrives from pcc itself and is correct here -- EDG emits
# real `sizeof' expressions rather than the 132 baked-in sizes cfront's
# C carried, so kencc computes every layout and conforming layout is
# exactly what the generated code wants.

OFILES=\
